}
Q.public_trust -= 6;
Q.early_election_risk = 100;
!}

= No fourth attempt

The constitutional sequence is exhausted. The President must shorten the term
of the Sejm and order an election. This is not a discretionary threat and not a
presidential cabinet system: there is simply no government with parliamentary
confidence.

- @formation_exit: Enter the campaign

@governing_agreement
title: Write rules for an impossible coalition
new-page: true
view-if: left_in_government = 1

= January 2024 — four parties, more than four parties

The cabinet contains KO's liberal core and local-government wing, Hołownia's
movement, PSL's agrarian machine, New Left's barons and younger progressive
women—and perhaps Razem ministers. A coalition document between party logos is
not enough. Each mini-party needs a way to lose a dispute without treating it
as grounds to leave.

PSL insists that every annual budget is a new confidence test. The Left knows
that accepting this principle gives a **[+ psl_seats +]-seat partner**
permanent leverage. It also knows that **[+ coalition_democratic_seats -
psl_seats +] is not 231**.

- @agreement_dispute_protocol
- @agreement_bilateral
- @agreement_majority_claim

@agreement_dispute_protocol
title: Create a written coalition and caucus dispute protocol
subtitle: Cost: 1 party resource. Slow bargaining, fewer surprise ultimatums.
